{"text": "Day had broken cold and gray when the man turned off the main Yukon trail and climbed the high bank of the frozen river. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It was nine oclock, but there was no sun or hint of sun, and a strange gloom lay over the white land. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The strangeness of it all made no impression on the man, a newcomer in the land, for this was his first winter there. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Fifty degrees below zero meant eighty odd degrees of frost to him, and that fact seemed only cold and uncomfortable. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The trouble with him was that he had no imagination, so the cold never made him think about his own weakness as a human. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To test the cold, he spat, and the spit crackled sharply in the air before it could fall to the snow. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He knew that spit crackled on the snow at fifty below, so it was surely colder than that, but how much colder he did not know. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He was heading for an old claim on Henderson Creek, where the boys were already waiting, and he would be there by six oclock. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> His lunch of biscuits was wrapped in a handkerchief and carried inside his shirt, against his bare skin, to keep it from freezing.", "alignment": {"characters": ["D", "a", "y", " ", "h", "a", "d", " ", "b", "r", "o", "k", "e", "n", " ", "c", "o", "l", "d", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "g", "r", "a", "y", " ", "w", "h", "e", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "m", "a", "n", " ", "t", "u", "r", "n", "e", "d", " ", "o", "f", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "m", "a", "i", "n", " ", "Y", "u", "k", "o", "n", " ", "t", "r", "a", "i", "l", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "c", "l", "i", "m", "b", "e", "d", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "h", "i", "g", "h", " ", "b", "a", "n", "k", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "r", "o", "z", "e", "n", " ", "r", "i", "v", "e", "r", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", 